{
 "generated_by": "proto/run_baselines.py",
 "protocol": "Run baselines.py: identical cross-store episode protocol to run_episodes_v3.py -- Begin() at the writer clock -> real relational read of row r -> query derived from that read -> 20ms think (writes commit) -> two retrievals at token S -> validate. A4 torn scored against the episode's OWN relational read; A5 is K1 != K2 at the same token. One episode active at a time (single-reader prototype). Maintenance period P=250 commits.",
 "maintenance_delay_definition": "A maintenance point becomes DUE every P=250 commits since the last applied compaction. Its delay is apply_time - due_time in commits (the logical clock). Reported mean/max/p99 over applied points, plus the count of points still unapplied at run end (accumulation check).",
 "policies": {
  "async500": "Append-only asynchronous index, lag L=500 commits; never compacts. No maintenance operator -> delay 0 by construction, which is exactly why it is the anomaly-ridden reference.",
  "lock": "Global lock serialises reads against in-flight embedding work; index always the current compacted state. Compaction inline, delay 0; every retrieval waits for the lock.",
  "scr": "Compaction staged and published at epoch boundaries; each snapshot pins one published generation. Publication immediate -> delay ~0; zero anomalies by construction; retains G=7 generations at 1.38x whole-index footprint (measured, Table 5 convention).",
  "quiesce": "B1: a due compaction is DEFERRED while an episode is active; the index keeps serving the current (uncompacted) adjacency. Applied when no episode is active. No drain guard (max_defer=None) -- i.e. the pure 'no compaction while episodes run' rule. Zero extra space (one index copy).",
  "double_buffer": "B2: maintenance builds a PRIVATE copy of the whole index and swaps atomically. Policy: a swap is only performed when no episode spans it (no episode active); an episode that would span the swap is DELAYED until the swap completes and is charged the extra latency. Peak space = 2x the non-versioned index (the private copy co-resident with the live one)."
 },
 "space_convention": "native_bytes = n_rows*(DIM*4 + M*4) with DIM=64, M=12: embeddings (float32) + graph adjacency (int32), i.e. the paper's memory_scope.py convention (embeddings + adjacency, no provenance). We report the retention POLICY per scheme rather than the prototype's raw index_bytes(), because every prototype index appends one entry per version (N+W entries) and would inflate all schemes equally. SCR's paper figure (1.38x whole index, 7.00x naive) is reproduced from memory_scope.py on testbed T2 (N=5000, G=7) and quoted here as the paper's convention; quiesce/lock retain exactly one index copy (1.00x); double-buffer peaks at 2.00x (live + private copy); async is reported as its measured append count / N.",
